Z||000000||Loki||10-16-2001||04:26 PM||||Just wondering if there any good? AC Delcos #1's, rapidfires, trying to justify $3.99 a pop. Any suggestions?<BR><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://members.home.net/fieroloki/loki_sig.gif">    <IMG SRC="http://members.home.net/fieroloki/w4[1].gif"> <BR>ICQ# 16477998||||reg||1
Z||000001||rogergarrison||10-16-2001||05:04 PM||||I only use single tip plugs, since only one fires at a time anyway. Ive always used Bosch Platinum, but trying a set of ACDelco i put in this summer. They seem to run ok but idle was smoother with the Bosch. Id stick with the $1.50 plugs.<P>------------------<BR>         <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=1234884&a=11878523&p=52990885"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Loki||10-16-2001||06:52 PM||||Well these are single tip..But ill look into the Bosch. Thanx<BR><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://members.home.net/fieroloki/loki_sig.gif">    <IMG SRC="http://members.home.net/fieroloki/w4[1].gif"> <BR>ICQ# 16477998||||reg||1
Z||000003||Kasdan||10-16-2001||07:16 PM||||i use bosch platinum plugs and bosch premium wires on mine, works like a champ.||||reg||1
Z||000004||mrfiero||10-16-2001||07:45 PM||||I put a set of AC Delco Rapidfires on my '88 GT and didn't notice any improvement.  I switched back to the Bosch platinums a month later because I have always had good luck with them and the idle seemed smoother.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Two88GTs||10-16-2001||10:29 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Loki:<BR><B>Just wondering if there any good? AC Delcos #1's, rapidfires, trying to justify $3.99 a pop. Any suggestions?<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I have Bosch +4s in my 71k GT and RapidFires in my 64k GT.  All of the "old" plugs in both cars(AC and Champion units, respectively) were in pretty good condition so I really didn't see a big improvement(although the firewall side plugs were rusting badly so I consider the new plugs to be preventative maintenance.)<P>Both cars idle well, I imagine both cars would run just as well with any new plug. For what it's worth, if I had to do it again, I would not spend $4-6/plug.  I'd probably buy regular Bosch platinums.  YMMV.||||reg||1
Z||000006||Rick 88||10-17-2001||12:48 AM||||When I got my 88 GT I did a tune up with Rapidfires. I pulled out Bosch Platinums. I don't know how long they had been there, but they looked fine. Now the engine idles better and throttle response is quicker. I can't say if it was just the plugs since I replaced the cap, rotor, set timing, and cleaned the throttle body. Either plug shoud do fine. Anyone have experience with Bosch Plus 4's ?<P>Rick 88||||reg||1
